<p class="lede">This site explains the State Pension, the yearly increase known as the triple lock, what a pension can cover, and the evidence for and against changing the rules. It is written for people who have heard these things in the news and want them explained.</p>

<h2 id="where-you-stand">Find where you stand</h2>

<p>Which State Pension a person gets depends on their date of birth, and for people born before <time datetime="1953-04-06">6 April 1953</time> on whether they are a man or a woman. When they can claim it depends on their date of birth. Men born before <time datetime="1951-04-06">6 April 1951</time> and women born before <time datetime="1953-04-06">6 April 1953</time> are on the basic State Pension. Everyone born later is on the new State Pension. {{ m.c("which-system") }}</p>

<p>The table shows State Pension age under the law today. It is not a check of your own entitlement. For that, use GOV.UK's <a href="https://www.gov.uk/state-pension-age">State Pension age calculator</a> and <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-state-pension">State Pension forecast</a>.</p>

